    <string name="terms_title">Terms of use and privacy notice</string>
    <string name="terms_updated">Version 2 · Effective 17 November 2026</string>
    <string name="terms_intro">Grace Ride (恩典同行) is a private ride-coordination app for PJ State CMC. It is not a public taxi or e-hailing service. You must opt in yourself. The box is never ticked for you.</string>
    <string name="terms_service_title">The service</string>
    <string name="terms_service_body">The app helps invited members arrange rides to church activities. An admin sends a link. You enter your own name and email. An admin later assigns your role and group. Until that approval, you can use your profile and nothing else.</string>
    <string name="terms_who_title">Who may join</string>
    <string name="terms_who_body">Use the app only with a link that was sent to you. Do not share your invite link or passkey. One person, one account. A parent or guardian must opt in for anyone under 18.</string>
    <string name="terms_controller_title">Who is responsible for your data</string>
    <string name="terms_controller_body">PJ State CMC decides how this app uses your personal data and is responsible for it. Send any question, request or complaint about your data to the church office or to an admin in the app.</string>
    <string name="terms_info_title">Information we collect</string>
    <string name="terms_info_body">Your name, email and phone, and a photo if you add one. Pickup addresses and ride times. Messages in a trip chat. If you claim costs: the payee name, phone or account you give, and receipt photos. We also keep a log of sign-ins and changes for security.</string>
    <string name="terms_sensitive_title">Sensitive information</string>
    <string name="terms_sensitive_body">Using this app shows that you take part in a church, and a ride may note a wheelchair, oxygen or other assistance need. The law treats religious belief and health as sensitive. By opting in you give your explicit consent for us to use this only to arrange your rides. Leave the assistance field empty if you prefer.</string>
    <string name="terms_purpose_title">Why we use it</string>
    <string name="terms_purpose_body">To identify you, approve your membership, match riders with drivers, contact you about a ride you are part of, share costs fairly, keep the app secure, and report attendance and transport to church leaders. We do not sell your data or use it for advertising.</string>
    <string name="terms_location_title">Rides and location</string>
    <string name="terms_location_body">A pickup address is shown to the assigned driver and the transport team when a ride is arranged. Live location is shared only while a trip is in progress, and it is deleted when the trip ends.</string>
    <string name="terms_see_title">Who can see your details</string>
    <string name="terms_see_body">There is no public member directory. A driver or passenger sees a phone number only for a ride they share, after that ride is approved. Admins, the transport team and the finance team see the records they need for their work.</string>
    <string name="terms_third_title">Map services outside Malaysia</string>
    <string name="terms_third_body">To find addresses and plan routes, the app sends addresses and map positions (never your name) to free OpenStreetMap services: Nominatim, OSRM and Photon. Your phone loads map images from OpenStreetMap. These servers may be outside Malaysia. Map data © OpenStreetMap contributors.</string>
    <string name="terms_retention_title">How long we keep it</string>
    <string name="terms_retention_body">Live location: until the trip ends. Trip chats: 180 days. Read notifications: 90 days; unread: one year. Security log: two years. Backups: 30 days. Your profile and ride history are kept while your account is open and for as long as church records require after it is closed.</string>
    <string name="terms_rights_title">Your rights</string>
    <string name="terms_rights_body">You can update your profile at any time. You can ask to see a copy of your data, correct it, receive it in a common format, or close your account. You can withdraw your consent, but you then cannot use the app. If you are not satisfied, you may complain to the Personal Data Protection Commissioner (JPDP).</string>
    <string name="terms_drivers_title">Drivers and riding</string>
    <string name="terms_drivers_body">Drivers are volunteers using their own cars. They must hold a valid licence, road tax and insurance, and drive safely. Riders pay no fare; any cost sharing only covers fuel and tolls at rates the church sets. Wear a seat belt and follow the driver’s safety directions. The church arranges rides in good faith but cannot guarantee any ride.</string>
    <string name="terms_conduct_title">Using the app properly</string>
    <string name="terms_conduct_body">Use other members’ details only to arrange the ride you share. Do not copy, share or misuse them. Be respectful in chats. Do not upload anything unlawful or anything you have no right to share. Admins may suspend an account that breaks these terms.</string>
    <string name="terms_ownership_title">Copyright</string>
    <string name="terms_ownership_body">The Grace Ride software and its design are protected by copyright and licensed to PJ State CMC. Do not copy, modify or redistribute them. The church’s name and logo belong to the church. Photos and messages you add stay yours; you allow the church to show them in the app for its ride work.</string>
    <string name="terms_changes_title">Changes to these terms</string>
    <string name="terms_changes_body">When these terms change in a way that matters, the version number changes and you are asked to opt in again before you continue.</string>
    <string name="terms_accept_title">How you opt in</string>
    <string name="terms_accept_body">Tick the box only after you have read these terms. We record the time and the version you agree to.</string>
    <string name="terms_opt_in">I have read these terms and the privacy notice, and I opt in</string>
    <string name="terms_agree">Agree and continue</string>
